[node name="Cover" type="Node3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "12 pieces, 6.0 x 1.5 x 3.0 m, grouped by radial lane. 3.0 m is the number the geometry demands, not a guess: the tower eye is at y=16.7, so the sightline onto a 1.7 m target 1.5 m behind a piece in the innermost lane (r=41, the steepest look-down angle on the map) passes 2.6 m above the deck. 3.0 m clears that with ~0.4 m to spare and still leaves a 3 m deep hiding pocket. Gaps between pieces are 22-28 deg (18-23 m of open ground) so the decision is when to cross, not how to weave."

